<%# Art. 13 GDPR / Art. 50 AI Act labelling, in two parts (Feinschliff P3).

    VISIBLE at all times: that the answers are AI-generated, and by whom. That is
    the sentence the AI Act asks for, and it is four words long.

    BEHIND the disclosure: where the input travels, under which jurisdiction, in
    which region, plus the second recipient when the search routes elsewhere.
    Those are the sentences that used to sit under every conversation permanently,
    and nobody read them twice.

    ⚠️ A NATIVE <details>, not a div driven by a controller (review of #625). The
    Art. 13 half must not depend on JavaScript: this app has already shipped a
    broken controller manifest to production once (root CLAUDE.md, "Stimulus
    Controller Index Bug"), and the privacy link in here is the ONLY one the chat
    surfaces have. With <details> the disclosure works with the controller absent,
    and Stimulus only adds the slide, Escape and click-beside.

    Two more things it gets for free, both of them findings in the first draft:
    the accessible name of the control IS its visible text (WCAG 2.5.3 — an
    aria-label reading "Hinweis zur KI-Verarbeitung anzeigen" over a control
    labelled "Details" is not reachable by voice), and there is no role="dialog"
    promising a focus trap that nothing implements.

    ⚠️ NO dom id, deliberately. This component renders on three surfaces, and the
    assistant panel renders on TOP of the two chat pages — a fixed id would collide
    with itself, which is a trap this codebase has walked into three times. <details>
    needs none: the element IS the state. %>
<details class="relative" data-controller="neo-ai-disclosure" data-action="toggle->neo-ai-disclosure#toggled">
  <%# text-muted, not text-faint: this line carries the one legally required
      statement that stays on screen, and it is also a control. Measured on white,
      --cream-500 gives 3.33:1 and --cream-600 gives 5.55:1; 1.4.3 AA asks 4.5:1 at
      this size (review of #625). list-none drops the native marker; the fold is
      told by the word "Details" instead. %>
  <summary class="text-xs text-muted list-none cursor-pointer select-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
    <i class="bi bi-info-circle mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_summary', provider: ai_provider_display_name) %>
    <span class="underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">
      <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_details') %>
    </span>
  </summary>

  <%# Above the summary (bottom-full) and sliding up into the conversation. The
      translation classes come OFF one frame after opening, so without JavaScript
      the note simply appears — the information is never behind the animation. %>
  <div data-neo-ai-disclosure-target="layer"
       class="absolute bottom-full inset-x-0 mb-2 z-10 translate-y-2 opacity-0 transition-all duration-200
              bg-surface-raised border-2 border-stroke rounded p-3 shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#000]">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold text-cream-900">
      <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_heading') %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">
      <% if package_jurisdiction %>
        <%# The jurisdiction labels are owned by the package catalogue's locale
            block — reusing them keeps the notice and the card literally the same
            claim (P5), which is the point of feeding both from the package. %>
        <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_package',
              provider: ai_provider_display_name,
              jurisdiction: t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.jurisdictions.#{package_jurisdiction}")) %>
        <% if package_processing_region %>
          <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_package_region',
                region: package_processing_region) %>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency', provider: ai_provider_display_name) %>
      <% end %>
      <% if embedding_provider_display_name_if_different %>
        <%= t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_embeddings',
              provider: embedding_provider_display_name_if_different) %>
      <% end %>
      <%= helpers.legal_page_link :privacy,
                                  label: t('views.organisations.chats.chat_show.ai_transparency_privacy_link'),
                                  target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener',
                                  class: 'underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2 hover:text-cream-900' %>
    </p>
  </div>
</details>
